<title>SPAIN: BBV named co-manager in ENI offer.</title>
<headline>BBV named co-manager in ENI offer.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish banking group Banco Bilbao Vizcaya (BBV) has been named co-manager in the international tranche of the second offering of shares in Italian state energy group Eni, the bank said on Monday.</p>
<p>It said the offer is to take place at the end of October or the beginning of November, and the placement has a value of around 500 billion pesetas.</p>
<p>BBV said it is the only Spanish bank to be included in the placement.</p>
<p>Lead managers in the deal are CS First Boston and Instituto Mobiliare Italiano, BBV said.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
